# Performance Optimization Analysis

After reviewing the codebase, I've identified several performance optimization opportunities. Here are my findings and actionable suggestions:

## 1. Unnecessary Re-renders & Redundant Computations

### Issue: MonthlyReport.tsx recalculates values on every render
In `MonthlyReport.tsx`, the `year`, `month`, `daysInMonth`, and `monthName` variables are recalculated on every render, even though they only depend on `selectedMonth` which changes infrequently.

### Solution: Memoize expensive calculations
```typescript
// Add these useMemo hooks
const [year, month] = useMemo(() => selectedMonth.split('-').map(Number), [selectedMonth]);
const daysInMonth = useMemo(() => new Date(year, month, 0).getDate(), [year, month]);
const monthName = useMemo(() => new Date(year, month - 1).toLocaleString('en-US', { month: 'long' }), [year, month]);
```

### Issue: monthOptions array recreated on every render
The `monthOptions` array is rebuilt on every render in `MonthlyReport.tsx`.

### Solution: Memoize the monthOptions array
```typescript
const monthOptions = useMemo(() => {
  const options = [];
  const now = new Date();
  for (let m = 0; m < 12; m++) {
    const val = `${now.getFullYear()}-${String(m + 1).padStart(2, '0')}`;
    const label = new Date(now.getFullYear(), m).toLocaleString('en-US', { month: 'long', year: 'numeric' });
    options.push({ value: val, label });
  }
  return options;
}, []); // Only depends on current year which doesn't change during session
```

## 2. Caching Opportunities

### Issue: No client-side caching for data fetching
Both `Dashboard.tsx` and `MonthlyReport.tsx` refetch all data on every refresh, even if the data hasn't changed significantly.

